              <description>GPB Input Signal De-bounce Enable Bit\nThe DBEN bit is used to enable the de-bounce function for each corresponding IO. If the input signal pulse width cannot be sampled by continuous two de-bounce sample cycle, the input signal transition is seen as the signal bounce and will not trigger the wake-up.  The de-bounce clock source is the 10 kHz internal low speed RC oscillator.\nThe de-bounce function is valid only for edge triggered.</description>
